  "question": {
    "text": "An object, moving with a speed of $6.25 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$, is decelerated at a rate given by :\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{dv}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=-2.5 \\sqrt{\\mathrm{v}}\n$$\nwhere $v$ is the instantaneous speed. The time taken by the object, to come to rest, would be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "szU9y",
      "text": "\n$2 \\mathrm{~s}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "hv3fU",
      "text": "\n$4 \\mathrm{~s}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iNnHF",
      "text": "\n$8 \\mathrm{~s}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XclCK",
      "text": "\n$1 \\mathrm{~s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\frac{d v}{d t}=-2.5 \\sqrt{v}\n$$\nIntegrating the above equation.\n$$\n\\Rightarrow 2 \\sqrt{v}=-2.5 \\mathrm{t}+\\mathrm{C}\n$$\nat $\\mathrm{t}=0, \\mathrm{v}=6.25 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{C}=5$\nat $v=0 \\Rightarrow t=\\frac{5}{2.5}=2 \\mathrm{~s}$",
    "image": null
  },
